## Muddy children (muddy-children): generated by spec_backend.py (WorldSpec, path B: Lean description, Python rules) from the instructor statements.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##  1. Three children are playing. Two of them, Amy and Ben, have mud on their foreheads; Cal does not.
##  2. Each child can see the other children's foreheads but not his or her own.
##  3. Their father says to all of them: "At least one of you has mud on your forehead."
##  4. Then he asks, again and again: "Do you know whether you have mud on your forehead?" All the children answer at the same time, truthfully, "yes" or "no".
##  5. Every child reasons perfectly and knows that the others do too, and every child hears every answer.
##  6. The goal is to find in which round each child first answers "yes", and why.
##
## Assumption ledger:
##   A-MC1: The eight possible patterns of mud are world objects; muddy and clean say each child's forehead in each world; view-mate(c, w, w2) holds when w2 differs from w only on c's own forehead (what c cannot see). The actual world is w-mmc.
##   A-MC2: Knowledge is explicit (JL, 16 Nov 2026): knows-at(c, w, r) holds when, in world w at round r, no world c cannot tell from w is still possible. It and the other derived relations use negation only in their definitions; operators test them positively.
##   A-MC3: The father's statement and each round are operators that rule out worlds (out-at(w, round)), on every world at once. A world is live at round r if it was not ruled out in an earlier round, so each round is judged on the worlds left before it. A stage number keeps the order; round objects carry their number.
##   A-MC4: A round records which children answer yes in the actual world (said-yes(c, r)), and rules out every world where some child would answer differently than in the actual world (all answers are heard).
##   A-MC5: The goal is that every child has answered yes in some round; the rounds of first yes are read from said-yes. Four rounds are provided.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute child 18
production optimize-attribute round 18
production optimize-attribute stage 18
production optimize-attribute task 18
production optimize-attribute object 18
production optimize-attribute muddy 12
production optimize-attribute clean 12
production optimize-attribute view-mate 24
production optimize-attribute actual 2
production optimize-attribute out-at 2
production optimize-attribute said-yes 2


## Propose initialize-muddy-children when its conditions below hold.
sp {muddy-children*propose*initialize-muddy-children
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-muddy-children ^task-operator false)
}

